What is a Baby Sling?
Baby Slings are fabric carriers designed to hold infants or toddlers close to the caregiver's body, enabling hands-free mobility while ensuring comfort and safety. Available in various styles including horizontal, front-facing, and back-type configurations, these products cater to different carrying preferences across age groups. Modern slings incorporate advanced ergonomic designs that support proper spinal and hip development in infants, making them increasingly popular among health-conscious parents.
